    not_duplicate_of: []  # 8ad1
    pr_ref:  # 8ad1
    description: "FOUND IN PASSING during the WI-hazop census, which adjudicated 332 auto-source\nrows against ADR-0049 ruling 1. These are NOT deferred crossings and ADR-0049\ndoes not reach them. They are ordinary misdeclarations of a different kind,\nfiled together because they were found by one sweep and share one root cause:\na row's boundary was chosen by what the call is ABOUT rather than by what it\nDOES.\n\nEach is a live false source or a false surface, because every boundary below\nauto-derives a taint source via AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP.\n\n  1. erlang `inet.gethostname` -- declared net_recv. It reads the LOCAL\n     hostname. Nothing crosses the network boundary; the value is host\n     DESCRIPTION. Correct boundary: host_info_read, which is the split\n     INV-tutar made for exactly this confusion (134 of 195 env_read rows were\n     host description, driving host-secret-* claims to 22.9% precision).\n\n  2. objc `NSNotificationCenter.removeObserver:` and\n     `removeObserver:name:object:` -- declared ipc_recv. UN-registering an\n     observer receives nothing and crosses nothing. Not even a deferred\n     crossing: there is no arrival being arranged, there is an arrival being\n     cancelled. Straight deletion, no representation question.\n\n  3. python `os.wait`, `os.wait3`, `os.wait4`, `os.waitid`, `os.waitpid` --\n     declared ipc_recv. They return a child's EXIT STATUS and resource usage,\n     not an IPC payload. A status integer the kernel computed is not data\n     another process sent. Nearest correct reading is host_info_read, or no\n     row at all.\n\n  4. python `sqlite3.Connection.backup` -- declared db_read. It WRITES the\n     database to another connection. Wrong direction: db_write.\n\n  5. erlang `ets.info`, `mnesia.table_info` -- declared db_read. They return\n     TABLE METADATA (size, memory, type), not stored rows. Reading a table's\n     shape is not reading its contents, and treating it as untrusted_input\n     mints taint from a number the runtime computed.\n\nWHY THEY ARE FILED TOGETHER RATHER THAN AS FIVE ITEMS. One sweep, one shape of\nerror, and the fix for each is a one-line boundary change or a deletion. Filed\nseparately they would be five P3s nobody batches; filed together they are one\nreviewable diff with five independent justifications.\n\nEVIDENCE OWED BEFORE ANY ROW MOVES, same bar as the family:\n  * a reachability fixture per row (the flask.Flask.run lesson -- a row can be\n    argued about at length while minting nothing);\n  * for the DELETIONS (removeObserver, os.wait*) the F2/F3 licence question is\n    trivial -- nothing is being relocated because nothing crosses -- but say so\n    in the PR rather than assuming it;\n  * for the RETAGS (gethostname -> host_info_read, backup -> db_write) confirm\n    the destination boundary does not itself auto-derive a source that makes\n    the situation worse. host_info_read DOES auto-derive (label\n    host_description), so gethostname stays a source and only changes label."  # 8ad1
    fields: {}  # 8ad1
- op: discuss  # 07f4
  at: '2026-08-30T05:59:48Z'  # 07f4
  by: agent  # 07f4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 07f4
  clock: 2  # 07f4
  nonce: 07f4  # 07f4
  message: "A SIXTH MISDECLARATION, found by measurement 0010 while adjudicating live findings: ets:foldl is a TRANSFER, not a callback-delivered deferred crossing.\n\n0009's register put it under CALLBACK with 'nothing; the data goes to a function you passed'. It does -- AND IT RETURNS THE ACCUMULATOR to its caller, whose content is computed by that function from the table's rows. That is ADR-0049 ruling 1's YES branch: the call returns, to its own caller, a value whose content the far side chose. It is unlike ftplib.FTP.retrbinary, which returns the server's response STATUS and no data at all, and unlike ets.foldr only in name.\n\nrabbitmq's own use makes the return load-bearing:\n  deps/rabbitmq_prometheus/src/collectors/prometheus_rabbitmq_core_metrics_collector.erl:640\n  {Table, A1, A2, A3, A4} = ets:foldl(fun({_, Props}, {T, A1, A2, A3, A4}) -> ...\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR 0010, disclosed there rather than absorbed: 15 situations -- 23% of the raw family join -- moved OUT of the deferred-crossing family on this correction, the same way 0009 held its 14 misdeclared rows out rather than folding a different bug into ADR-0049's.\n\nNOT RE-CHECKED, and named so it is not assumed: dets:traverse is the same shape (a fun plus an accumulated result) and produced no findings in this cohort, so it is untested here. ets:foldr was not examined either."  # 07f4
